  <subsection xml:id="unit1-project1-roadtrip">
    <title>Project 1: Road Trip Budget Planner</title>
   
    <p>A family is planning a road trip and wants to estimate fuel costs, food costs, and 
        see if they qualify for a random travel discount. You will write code to plan their road trip budget.
    </p>

  <p>Program Requirements: Ask the user for the following information and store the input into variables.
  </p>
  <ul>`
    <li>Driver's name</li>
    <li>Total trip miles</li>
    <li>Vehicle miles per gallon</li>
    <li>Gas price per gallon</li>
    <li>Number of travelers</li>
    <li>Food budget per person</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Calculate the following and store the results into variables:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Gallons of gas needed</li>
    <li>Fuel cost</li>
    <li>Total food cost</li>
    <li>Total trip cost</li>
    <li>Average cost per traveler</li>
    <li>Whole number of gas stops (assume there will be a stop every 120 miles)</li>
    <li>Remaining miles after the last full gas stop</li>
    <li>Random discount between 5% and 20% (divide by 100 to convert to decimal)</li>
    <li>Discounted total</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Display a formatted trip summary (see sample below).</p>
<pre>
Sample output:
---------------------------------
ROAD TRIP SUMMARY
—------------------------------
Driver: Maria
Number of Travelers: 4
Gas Needed: 30.18 gallons
Fuel Cost: $108.35
Food Cost: $220.00
Total Cost: $328.35
Average Cost Per Traveler: $82.09
Random Discount: 14%
Discounted Cost: $282.38
Estimated Gas Stops: 8
Miles After Last Stop: 45
</pre>


  <activity label="unit1-project1-roadtrip">
  <statement>
    <p>Calculate a road trip budget from the inputs of driver name, total trip miles, vehicle miles 
        per gallon, gas price per gallon, number of travelers, and food budget per person. Calculate
        the gallons of gas needed, fuel cost, total food cost, total trip cost, average cost per traveler,
        whole number of gas stops, remaining miles after the last full gas stop, random discount,
        and discounted total. Display a formatted trip summary like below.
        Please use the variables provided in the starting code below.
        Run your code at least once with the following input for autograding: 
        <pre>
Sample input: Pat, 200, 30, 4.00, 3, 15
---------------------------------
ROAD TRIP SUMMARY
---------------------------------
Driver: Pat
Number of Travelers: 3
Gas Needed: 6.67 gallons
Fuel Cost: $26.67
Food Cost: $45.00
Total Cost: $71.67
Average Cost Per Traveler: $23.89
Random Discount: 13%
Discounted Cost: $62.35
Estimated Gas Stops: 1
Miles After Last Stop: 80.00
        </pre>
    </p>
</statement>
<program interactive="activecode" language="python">
<code>
import random

# 1. Input: get the following input from the user 
#    Convert the numerical inputs to float or int
driver = 
miles = 
mpg = 
gas_price = 
travelers = 
food_budget = 

# 2. Calculate the following
gallons_needed = 
fuel_cost = 
food_cost = 
total_cost = 
average_cost = 
gas_stops = 
remaining_miles = 

# 3. Generate a random discount from 5% to 20% using random.randint() 
#    Divide by 100 to convert to decimal
discount =

# 4. Calculate the discounted amount and total 
discount_amount = 
discounted_total = 

# 5. Print the results of all of calculations (see sample output above)
</code>
<tests>
from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui

class myTests(TestCaseGui):

    def testOne(self):
        code = self.getEditorText().replace(" ", "")
        self.assertIn("miles/mpg", code, "gallons_needed can be calculated using miles, mpg, and /")
        self.assertIn("gallons_needed*gas_price",code,"fuel_cost can be calculated using gallons_needed, gas_price, and *.")
        self.assertIn("travelers*food_budget",code,"food_cost can be calculated using travelers, food_budget, and *.")
        self.assertIn("total_cost/travelers",code,"average_cost can be calculated using total_cost, travelers, and /.")
        self.assertIn("miles//120",code,"gas_stops can be calculated using miles, 120, and //.")
        self.assertIn("miles%120",code,"remaining_miles can be calculated using miles, 120, and %.")
        self.assertIn("random.randint(5,21)",code,"discount can be generated using random.randint(5, 21).")
        self.assertIn("total_cost-discount_amount",code,"discounted_total can be calculated using total_cost and discount_amount.")
        self.assertIn("23.8", str(average_cost), "average_cost starts with 23.8 if you enter the test case input: Pat, 200, 30, 4.00, 3, 15")
        self.assertNotIn("23.8", code, "23.8 should not be hard-coded in the code") 

myTests().main()
</tests>
</program>
</activity>

</subsection>


<subsection>
    <title>Unit 1 Coding Project 2: Event Invitation Generator</title>



<p>A community center is hosting its annual Community Fun Run and wants a program 
    that automatically creates personalized invitations and printable name badges for participants. 
    The program should personalize the invitation using information entered by the user.
    </p>

 <p>Program Requirements: Ask the user for the following information and store the input into 
    variables.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>First Name</li>
        <li>Last Name</li>
        <li>Favorite Hobby</li>
        <li>Favorite Color</li>
        <li>City</li>
    </ul>

    <p>In your code, create the following:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>A full name using string concatenation.</li>
        <li>Initials using the first letter of the first and last names.</li>
        <li><p>A Badge ID using:
            <ul>
                <li>First 3 letters of the first name</li>
                <li>First 3 letters of the last name</li>
                <li>Random two-digit number</li>
            </ul>
            </p></li>
        <li><p>An Invitation Code using:
            <ul>
                <li>First 2 letters of the city</li>
                <li>First 2 letters of the hobby</li>
                <li>Random three-digit number</li>
            </ul>
            </p></li>
        <li>A Lucky Prize Number (1–100).</li>

    </ul>

<p>Display the personalized invitation and name badge (see sample below).</p>

<pre>
Sample output:
Sample output:
===================================
Community Fun Run Invitation
===================================
Hello Dani Garcia!
You are officially invited to the Community Fun Run
October 12 at 9:00 AM
Riverside Park
Please wear something blue and be prepared
to share your favorite hobby: painting!
Invitation Code: Chpa428
Lucky Prize Number: 57
----------------------------------
NAME BADGE
----------------------------------
COMMUNITY FUN RUN
Name: Dani Garcia
Initials: DG
City: Chicago
Badge ID: DanGar84
----------------------------------
We look forward to seeing you!
</pre>


<activity label="unit1-project2-invitation">
  <statement>
    <p>Create a personalized invitation and name badge from the inputs of  
        first name, last name, favorite hobby, favorite color, and city. 
        Create the full name, initials, badge id, invitation code, and lucky number.
        Display a formatted invitation and name badge like below.
        Use the variables provided in the starting code below. Run it at least once 
        with the following input for auto-grading:
        <pre>
Input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago

Sample output:
===================================
Community Fun Run Invitation
===================================
Hello Dani Garcia!
You are officially invited to the Community Fun Run
October 12 at 9:00 AM
Riverside Park
Please wear something blue and be prepared
to share your favorite hobby: painting!
Invitation Code: Chpa428
Lucky Prize Number: 57
----------------------------------
NAME BADGE
----------------------------------
COMMUNITY FUN RUN
Name: Dani Garcia
Initials: DG
City: Chicago
Badge ID: DanGar84
----------------------------------
We look forward to seeing you!
</pre>
    </p>
    </statement>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python">
        <code>
import random

# 1. Input: get the following input from the user 
first_name =
last_name =
favorite_hobby =
favorite_color =
city =

# 2. Create the full name of the participant
fullname =

# 3. Get the initials (first letter of first name and first letter of last name)
initials =

# 4. Create the badge id for the participant
#    Use the first three letters of the first name, the first three letters of the last name, 
#    and a random two-digit number
badge_id =

# 5. Create the invitation code for the participant
#   Use the first two letters of the city, the first two letters of the hobby, 
#   and a random three-digit number
invitation_code =

# 6. Calculate a random lucky number for the participant from 1 - 100
lucky_number =
# print out the invitation and the name badge using the sample output above as a guide

</code>
<tests>
from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui

class myTests(TestCaseGui):

    def testOne(self):
        code = self.getEditorText().replace(" ", "")
        self.assertIn("first_name+\" \"+last_name", code, "fullname concatenates first_name, \" \", and last_name.")
        self.assertIn("first_name[0]", code, "first_name[0] gets the first letter of first_name for the initials")
        self.assertIn("first_name[0:3]",code,"first_name[0:3] gets the first 3 letters of first_name.")
        self.assertIn("random.randint(10",code,"random.randint used starting at 10 for a 2-digit number")
        self.assertIn("city[0:2]",code,"city[0:2] gets the first two letters of the city.")
        self.assertIn(favorite_color, self.getOutput(), "favorite_color should be printed in the invitation.")
        self.assertIn("DanGar", self.getOutput(), "Badge ID should start with DanGar for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")
        self.assertIn("Chpa", self.getOutput(), "Invitation Code should start with Chpa for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")
        self.assertIn("Dani Garcia", self.getOutput(), "Full name should be printed in the invitation for the test case input: Dani, Garcia, painting, blue, Chicago")
        self.assertNotIn("Dani Garcia", code, "Dani Garcia should not be hard-coded in the code") 
myTests().main()
</tests>
</program>
</activity>


